<div class="lab-obs bz" data-l10n="" data-en="&lt;b&gt;👀 Try this: &lt;/b&gt;degree 1 → underfitting (a straight line can’t fit the curve); degree 3–4 → just right; degree 9 + long training → overfitting (the curve passes through every blue dot, but the orange validation error goes up). Drag the learning rate all the way right → divergence. When it overfits, try setting weight decay to 0.01." data-bz="1"><div class="bz-h"><b>👀 Try this: </b></div><ul class="pts"><li>degree 1 → underfitting (a straight line can’t fit the curve)</li><li>degree 3–4 → just right</li><li>degree 9 + long training → overfitting (the curve passes through every blue dot, but the orange validation error goes up).</li><li>Drag the learning rate all the way right → divergence.</li><li>When it overfits, try setting weight decay to 0.01.</li></ul></div>
